# 9. LEVEL 4 — ARCHITECTURAL CONFORMANCE

Only after the mathematical model has been sufficiently verified.

Now compare:

$$
\text{Theory}
\rightarrow
\text{Computational Model}
\rightarrow
\text{Architecture}
\rightarrow
\text{Implementation}
$$

For each mapping ask:

1. What mathematical object is being implemented?
2. Where is it represented?
3. What architectural component realizes it?
4. What invariant is preserved?
5. What assumptions are introduced?
6. Is anything lost?
7. Is anything added?
8. Does implementation behaviour correspond to the formal semantics?

Never reason:

> implementation does X → therefore theory means X.

That direction is forbidden unless separately justified.

