# 18. FINAL PRINCIPLE

The objective is not to prove the book.

The objective is not to prove the architecture.

The objective is to discover whether there exists a **coherent, mathematically and statistically defensible KnowledgeOS theory**, and then determine whether it is computationally realizable and architecturally implementable.

The final desired chain is:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Definitions}
\rightarrow
\text{Axioms/Assumptions}
\rightarrow
\text{Derivations}
\rightarrow
\text{Mathematical Theory}
\rightarrow
\text{Statistical Theory}
\rightarrow
\text{Computational Model}
\rightarrow
\text{Efficient Algorithms}
\rightarrow
\text{Architecture}
}
$$

Only what survives this chain should eventually become part of a **Final KnowledgeOS Theory**.

Edition 2 is the candidate baseline.

This Verify Session determines what, if anything, deserves to survive into the final theory.
